You say you shoot all the bar stuff, you shoot on the apartment stuff, you shoot all Robin and a cab stuff, and you sort of, we have three days where Susie Greenberg and Pam Freeman, our director and our amazing crew, have to sort of like jenga or whatever puzzle piece that together.
你说你拍完所有酒吧的戏，拍完公寓的戏，拍完所有罗宾在出租车里的戏，然后我们有三天时间，苏西·格林伯格和我们的导演帕姆·弗里曼（Pam Freeman）以及我们惊艳的工作人员，必须像玩层层叠或者拼图那样把它们拼凑起来。

00:18:07.933 --> 00:18:09.970
How do you make that all fit into three days?
你怎么能把所有这些塞进三天里？

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:40.369
This one has the illusion of seeming like there's more going on than there really is because it really is mostly the bar and the apartment You see the bars you see the bathroom in the bar, which isn't doesn't always happen Yeah, you see Ted's bedroom, which they had to they had to fly that in because that's not like just sitting there offstage It was in a whole different little area of the stage, you know, just another shout out to Susie Greenberg It occurs to me and maybe it's just because I've been watching the pit that she would have been a great emergency room doctor because she is unflappable.
这一集给人一种“事情比实际更多”的错觉，因为它实际上大部分都在酒吧和公寓里。你看到了酒吧，你看到了酒吧里的洗手间——这可不常发生。对，你看到了泰德的卧室，他们不得不把那个布景空运进来，因为那不是那种就放在那儿不用的东西，它在舞台的一个完全不同的区域，你知道的，再次向苏西·格林伯格致敬。我突然想到，也许只是因为我看过那部剧，她会是一个极好的急诊室医生，因为她太沉着冷静了。我从未见过苏西·格林伯格显得压力山大，或者觉得“哦，我们弄不灵清了”。就像她从不惊慌。我知道为什么她能处于职业生涯的巅峰。她绝对就是能把事情搞定。

00:18:40.369 --> 00:18:48.390
I never saw Susie Greenberg look stressed or like, oh, we're not gonna figure this out.
