00:20:56.866 --> 00:21:08.579
We need to shoot all this stuff on a Wednesday, but in this one on shooting all the drunk stuff first was actually quite helpful because by the time I was doing it on Thursday, I kind of had that in my bloodstream.
（重复索引278的翻译）

00:21:08.579 --> 00:21:09.420
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:10.980
It was useful.
很有用。

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:12.299
It was useful the order.
这个顺序很有用。

00:21:12.299 --> 00:21:18.779
And I think that Susie and Pam did try to pay attention to that as much as they could, but you can't always get it just right.
我觉得苏西和帕姆确实尽量去注意这一点，但你不可能每次都安排得刚刚好。

00:21:18.779 --> 00:21:20.740
I guarantee you they would have thought of that.
我敢保证她们肯定考虑过这一点。

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:24.740
I guarantee you they probably thought, Josh can be hung over these next two days.
我敢保证她们大概想过：“接下来这两天乔什宿醉，先让他喝醉吧。”

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:26.259
Let's have him drunk first.
这就是叙事的顺序。

00:21:26.259 --> 00:21:28.180
That's just the narrative order.
我敢保证帕姆非常擅长考虑诸如此类的事情，因为帕姆真的能站在演员的角度去思考。

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:34.140
I guarantee you that Pam is great at thinking about stuff like that because Pam could really think in the actors' shoes.
她是一位出色的导演，因为她真的会思考：他们会想怎么演这场戏？我无法告诉你，我想我在播客里提到过，我无法告诉你我们有多少次在清晨一上班就拍清晨的戏，因为我记得来上班时不得不换上睡衣或者T恤和运动裤，然后戴夫·贝克（Dave Baker）会问：“你想吃什么麦片？吃什么早餐？咖啡要怎么做？”

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:38.019
She's a wonderful director because she really thinks how will they want to play this?
就像，然后我就觉得：这是世界上最棒的工作。

00:21:38.019 --> 00:21:59.579
And I can't tell you how many times, I think I've mentioned this in the podcast, I can't tell you how many times we did early morning scenes first thing in the morning, because I remember coming to work and having to get in pajamas or a t-shirt and sweatpants and Dave Baker being like, what cereal do you want, what breakfast, how do you want your coffee?
就像，现在才早上9点。

00:21:59.579 --> 00:22:01.900
Like, and I was just like, this is the greatest job in the world.
我在喝咖啡、吃麦片，还跟杰森聊天。

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:03.660
Like, it's 9 a.m.
就像，你知道的，我当时只是在和杰森瞎胡闹，然后摄像机开始运转，而我还在和杰森瞎胡闹。

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:07.619
I'm drinking coffee and eating cereal and talking to Jason.
这只是我们有必须说出来的台词。

00:22:07.619 --> 00:22:13.099
Like, you know, I was just messing around with Jason and then the cameras roll and I'm still messing around with Jason.
